<Project>

  <Import Project="$([MSBuild]::GetPathOfFileAbove('Directory.Build.targets', '$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)..'))" />

  <!--
    Canonical product-coverage exclusion whitelist (reviewed 2026-07-14, moved from coverage.runsettings
    when the suites left VSTest): compiler/OpenAPI/protobuf generated types, *.g.cs files and obj/
    outputs, and the EF migration history generated by tooling. Every handwritten source file,
    including Program.cs, design-time infrastructure, logging providers, Blazor components, agent
    collectors and hosted services, remains in the denominator. E2E execution is separate evidence,
    never a coverage exclusion.

    coverlet.MTP reads it from testconfig.json next to the test executable, only when a run turns
    coverage on (the coverlet switch). A present file is authoritative (coverlet injects none of its
    own defaults), which is what keeps the measured denominator the one coverlet.collector measured.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)testconfig.json" Link="testconfig.json"
          CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest" Visible="false" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
